    "body": "I think \r\n\r\n `getter (HTMLAppletElement or HTMLEmbedElement or HTMLFormElement or HTMLIFrameElement or HTMLImageElement or HTMLObjectElement or WindowProxy or HTMLCollection) (DOMString name)`\r\n\r\nis definitely way overkill, particularly since there's very little difference between `HTMLElement` and its various subclasses (only a few properties/methods each).\r\n\r\nI think `object` is overly generic and suggests that absolutely any sort of object might be returned, and should be used only where needed.  I don't think there's any need for clarity to spell out exactly which subinterfaces can be returned, it's fine to include a bunch of derived interfaces in one base.\r\n\r\nI would like it the way I suggested it partly because I think it would make Gecko's code to implement this method look a lot nicer and easier to read.  I don't know if this counts for much.  :)  ",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
